# Data Handling

## Raw Data — Read Only
- Files in `/data/raw/` are **never modified** — treat as read-only source of truth
- All cleaning logic lives exclusively in a dedicated utility module (e.g. `data_utils.py`)
- Cleaned outputs are written to `/data/processed/`

## Loading & Caching
- DataFrames are loaded once at app startup using FastAPI's `lifespan` event
- Never re-read CSV files per request — always serve from cached DataFrames
- Cache using a simple module-level dict or FastAPI app state

## Pandas Conventions
- Always specify `dtype` when reading CSVs to avoid silent type coercion
- Column names should be lowercase with underscores (e.g. `monthly_total`)
- Return plain dicts or lists from data functions — not DataFrames — for JSON serialisation

## Example pattern
```python
def get_summary_records() -> list[dict]:
    """Return records from the cached DataFrame as serialisable dicts."""
    df = _cache["summary"]  # loaded at startup via lifespan
    return df[["id", "label", "value"]].to_dict(orient="records")
```
